verdicts.corrected_statement:
If the adapter runs under native main.py/eval_policy.sh, several paths start a new layout or a new process automatically:
- an UnStableError, any generic exception, or a PhysXBroken abandon-and-refill moves on to the next layout;
- with eval_num 25, even a normal end of layout 0 continues to layout 1;
- a PhysXFatal re-exec (up to 3) or a bash retry (up to 10) re-runs the same layout 0 from scratch as a new attempt. The resume manifest records only completed and abandoned IDs, and an in-progress layout is neither.

Pinning one layout (eval_num=1 plus a manifest that abandons IDs 1-69, or installing only make_toast_0.json in seed dir 0) removes substitution. It does not remove the same-layout re-run. That also needs ROBODOJO_FATAL_RESTART_COUNT preset to 3 or more plus ROBODOJO_MAX_BASH_RETRIES=0, or a custom single-episode loop. All of these must end as infrastructure results.

